t_accum: a 32-bit value shifted right by 32 (SparkTar's and SparkCPIO's c/cat).

t_accum splits a value into bytes with n >> (i * 8) for i = 0..4.  A shift
of 32 is undefined in C; ARM's shifter gives 0 (what Norcroft's code relies
on), x86 and AArch64 take the count modulo 32, and clang at -O2 drops the
fifth byte: a date in an archive came out as 1900.  The shift is now done
only when it is under 32, else 0, as on ARM.

diff -ru a/SparkCPIO/cat.c b/SparkCPIO/cat.c
--- a/SparkCPIO/cat.c	2026-10-02 07:12:16.588652412 +0100
+++ b/SparkCPIO/cat.c	2026-10-02 07:12:16.606843048 +0100
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
         int i, j;
 
         for ( i = 0; i <= 4; ++i )
-                a[i] = ( n >> ( i * 8 ) & 0xFF );
+                a[i] = ( i < 4 ? n >> ( i * 8 ) & 0xFF : 0 ); /* ARM: >> 32 is 0 */
         for ( i = 0; i <= 4; ++i )
         {
                 n = mul * t->t[i] + a[i];
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@
                 t->t[i] = (n & 0xFF);
 
                 for ( j = i + 1; j <= 4; ++j )
-                        a[j] += ( n >> ( (j-i) * 8 ) & 0xFF );
+                        a[j] += ( j-i < 4 ? n >> ( (j-i) * 8 ) & 0xFF : 0 );
         }
 }
 
